  "term": "amobarbital",
  "definition": "Amobarbital is a barbiturate that acts as a sedative and sleep-inducing drug, rather than an antianxiety medication. Its main harms come from dose-related slowing of central nervous system activity, and ongoing use carries a high risk of dependence.",
